## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/cablesplit.html
- Summary (EN): Divides one cable into two outputs, matching and non_matching, using filters on name pattern, wire type, wire index range or random chance. Available since version 21.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Le nœud cablesplit sépare un câble en deux sorties, matching et non_matching, selon le motif de nom, le type, une plage d'index ou un tirage aléatoire.

- Inputs meaning: ["cable: the cable to split"]

- Key parameters: [{"name": "Split by Pattern / Name Pattern", "meaning": "Filters wires by name using Houdini pattern matching"}, {"name": "Split by Type / Type", "meaning": "Filters wires by data type; wires must match to reach matching"}, {"name": "Split by Range / Select", "meaning": "Picks every Nth wire (every other by default)"}, {"name": "Split by Range / Start, End", "meaning": "First and last wire indices of the range"}, {"name": "Split by Range / Offset", "meaning": "Subtracted from the wire index before the range check"}, {"name": "Split by Chance / Probability", "meaning": "Chance a wire goes to matching, given as a percentage"}, {"name": "Split by Chance / Seed", "meaning": "Changes the random result"}]

- Caveats: ["The page says the filters run sequentially and are unioned, yet also says that enabling both Pattern and Type requires a wire to satisfy both; verify in Houdini", "Probability is a percentage, but the page says a value of 1 selects all wires, which looks inconsistent; verify in Houdini", "Iteration idiom from the page: Select 1, of 1, Start 0, End 0, Offset C@cop_iteration"]

